---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Canada vs UK vs Australia Immigration Compared | AfriMigrate"
  description="A free, side-by-side comparison of Canada, UK and Australia skilled migration: cost, timeline, job offer requirements, and path to permanent residence."
>
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Compare</div>
  <div class="eyebrow">Compare Destinations</div>
  <h1>Canada vs UK vs Australia</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    All three are strong destinations for African professionals, but they work very differently. Here's how they stack up on the factors that matter most.
  </p>

  <section class="section">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>🇨🇦 Canada</th><th>🇬🇧 UK</th><th>🇦🇺 Australia</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Job offer required?</td><td>No (Express Entry)</td><td>Yes (Skilled Worker)</td><td>No (subclass 189)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>System type</td><td>Points-based (CRS)</td><td>Sponsor-led</td><td>Points-based</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Typical upfront cost</td><td>~CAD $2,500–4,000/family</td><td>~£3,000–6,000/family</td><td>~AUD $4,000–7,000/family</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Time to permanent residence</td><td>~6–24 months</td><td>~5 years to ILR</td><td>~12–24 months</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Provincial/state route</td><td>Provincial Nominee Program</td><td>Not applicable</td><td>State nomination (190/491)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Path to citizenship</td><td>~3 years after PR</td><td>~1 year after ILR</td><td>~4 years after PR</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px; margin-top: 1rem;">
      Figures are indicative and change over time — use our free tools for a more precise, personal estimate for each country.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Quick Take</div>
    <h2>Which one fits you?</h2>
    <div class="tools-grid">
      <div class="tool-card"><div class="tool-icon">🇨🇦</div><h3>Choose Canada if...</h3><p>You don't have a job offer yet and want the most transparent, points-based route to permanent residence.</p><a href="/canada" class="tool-link">Explore Canada →</a></div>
      <div class="tool-card"><div class="tool-icon">🇬🇧</div><h3>Choose the UK if...</h3><p>You already have (or can realistically get) a job offer from a licensed sponsor in your field.</p><a href="/uk" class="tool-link">Explore the UK →</a></div>
      <div class="tool-card"><div class="tool-icon">🇦🇺</div><h3>Choose Australia if...</h3><p>Your occupation is in demand and you want an independent, no-job-offer visa with strong long-term prospects.</p><a href="/australia" class="tool-link">Explore Australia →</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
